/*!
\page page_stsstHitCollection StSstHitCollection — Collection Documentation

\ref StSstHitCollection is the top-level container for all reconstructed Silicon
Strip Tracker (SST) hits in a single STAR event.  The SST was a refurbishment
and upgrade of the SSD, reusing the same barrel geometry with updated electronics.
Hits are organised in a three-level hierarchy: detector → ladder → wafer.

\see StSstHitCollection
\see StSstLadderHitCollection
\see StSstWaferHitCollection
\see StSstHit

---

\section sst_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
StSstHitCollection                 (top-level, one per event)
└── StSstLadderHitCollection         [20 ladders, indices 0–19]
    └── StSstWaferHitCollection        [up to 16 wafers per ladder, indices 0–15]
        └── StSPtrVecSstHit              (owns the StSstHit objects)
\endcode

All sub-collection nodes are embedded (stack-allocated) inside their parent;
no heap allocation is used for collection nodes.

\section sst_containment Containment Model

| Level    | Class                         | Contents                                  |
|----------|-------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
| Detector | \ref StSstHitCollection       | 20 \ref StSstLadderHitCollection objects  |
| Ladder   | \ref StSstLadderHitCollection | 16 \ref StSstWaferHitCollection objects   |
| Wafer    | \ref StSstWaferHitCollection  | `StSPtrVecSstHit` of `StSstHit*`          |

\section sst_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StSstWaferHitCollection holds its hits in a member of type
\c StSPtrVecSstHit, which is a **smart-pointer vector** that **owns** the
\ref StSstHit objects it contains.  The \ref StSstWaferHitCollection destructor
explicitly deletes every hit in the vector (necessary because \ref StSstHit
provides its own pool-allocated \c new/delete).

Ladder and wafer sub-collections are embedded members of their parent classes
and are destroyed automatically with the parent.  \ref StSstHitCollection itself
is owned by the StEvent framework (\c St_DataSet / \c StXRefMain).

\warning Do **not** delete individual \ref StSstHit pointers obtained from the
collection.  The collection manages their lifetimes.

\section sst_members Data Members

\subsection sst_members_top StSstHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StSstLadderHitCollection[20]` | `mLadders` | Fixed-size array of 20 ladder sub-collections. |

\subsection sst_members_ladder StSstLadderHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StSstWaferHitCollection[16]` | `mWafers` | Fixed-size array of up to 16 wafer sub-collections. |

\subsection sst_members_wafer StSstWaferHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StSPtrVecSstHit` | `mHits` | Smart-pointer vector of `StSstHit*`; owns all contained hits. |

\section sst_methods Key Methods

\subsection sst_methods_top StSstHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `addHit(StSstHit*)` | `bool` | Routes hit to correct ladder/wafer. Returns `false` if indices are out of range. |
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits across all ladders and wafers. |
| `numberOfLadders() const` | `unsigned int` | Always 20. |
| `ladder(unsigned int)` | `StSstLadderHitCollection*` | 0-based ladder access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection sst_methods_ladder StSstLadderHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits on this ladder. |
| `numberOfWafers() const` | `unsigned int` | Always 16. |
| `wafer(unsigned int)` | `StSstWaferHitCollection*` | 0-based wafer access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection sst_methods_wafer StSstWaferHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `hits()` | `StSPtrVecSstHit&` | Mutable reference to the hit vector. |
| `hits() const` | `const StSPtrVecSstHit&` | Const reference to the hit vector. |

\section sst_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StSstHitCollection* sstColl = event->sstHitCollection();
if (!sstColl) return;

for (unsigned int iLad = 0; iLad < sstColl->numberOfLadders(); ++iLad) {
    const StSstLadderHitCollection* ladderColl = sstColl->ladder(iLad);
    if (!ladderColl) continue;

    for (unsigned int iWaf = 0; iWaf < ladderColl->numberOfWafers(); ++iWaf) {
        const StSstWaferHitCollection* waferColl = ladderColl->wafer(iWaf);
        if (!waferColl) continue;

        const StSPtrVecSstHit& hits = waferColl->hits();
        for (const StSstHit* hit : hits) {
            // process hit ...
        }
    }
}
\endcode
*/
